  "content": {
    "title": "Will your mail arrive today? How USPS, UPS, FedEx handle Good Friday",
    "text": "April 3, 2026, 2:19 p.m. ETGood Friday is not a federal holiday, so most services operate as usual.The U.S. Postal Service will continue to deliver mail on Good Friday.UPS and FedEx will also maintain their normal pickup and delivery schedules.If you're waiting on a package to land this weekend, you might be wondering whether Good Friday will slow things down.Easter Sunday, one of Christianity's most significant holidays, falls on April 5 this year. The religious tradition takes place over several days a part of Holy Week, which includes Palm Sunday, Maundy Thursday, Good Friday, Holy Saturday and, of course, Easter.Good Friday, which falls on April 3 this year, commemorates the crucifixion and death of Jesus Christ. Countless churches across the state hold afternoon or evening services, prayer vigils and Stations of the Cross observances.With Good Friday observed by millions of Christians, many people wonder whether everyday services like mail delivery are affected. Here's what to know.Is mail delivered on Good Friday?Yes, mail delivery still takes place on Good Friday.Though it's widely observed by Christian churches, Good Friday is not a federal holiday, which means banks, mail delivery and most government offices remain open.U.S. Postal Service facilities maintain normal operations on Good Friday, which means retail transactions and mail delivery will go on as usual, according to the USPS website.UPS and FedEx are no different. The companies' pickup and delivery services are available throughout the day, and both stores' locations will be open, according to the UPS and FedEx company websites.Similarly, while some smaller businesses may tweak their hours for the holiday, most major retailers are open on Good Friday.Reporter Emma Wozniak can be reached at ewozniak@dispatch.com or @emma_wozniak_ on X, formerly known as Twitter.",
